WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.000
Help starts with a report.
A silent product walkthrough

2
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:20.000
See who needs attention.
Reported needs set the suggested order. Service-area filters help responders focus.

3
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:30.000
Turn words into a case.
Process a sample transcript through the backend. Three people. A specific landmark. A shelter need.

4
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:40.000
Keep the facts visible.
Beacon preserves the caller’s words and location, then explains suggested urgency and coverage.

5
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:48.000
Start with the current need.
A fictional caller reports three people safely waiting for shelter near Riverbend footbridge.

6
00:00:48.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Let new danger change priority.
The same fictional situation now includes rising indoor water and no safe exit. The continuing case is reassessed.

7
00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:12.000
Preserve how the situation changed.
Two linked reports remain available. The latest facts guide the current response without erasing the earlier report.

8
00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:26.000
Hold response for human review.
A fictional unsafe request has exact quoted evidence. Normal assignment and ETA are held; verification ownership remains possible.

9
00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:36.000
Make the decision accountable.
The reviewer records a reason against the current evidence before accepting the report for response.

10
00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:44.000
Acceptance opens the next step.
The decision is recorded with its evidence scope. Coverage and responder eligibility still require confirmation.

11
00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:52.000
Claiming establishes ownership.
An approved fictional team claims the accepted case. A claim alone does not confirm travel or arrival.

12
00:01:52.000 --> 00:02:00.000
Report an estimate explicitly.
Choose On the way and enter a fresh ten-minute estimate. The desk owns the status update.

13
00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:12.000
Be precise about reassurance.
Beacon shows who reported the update and when. Arrival remains an estimate; time passing never confirms arrival.

14
00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:20.000
Human decisions. Clear evidence.
Explore the manual, test cases, and system design on the product website.

